  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region in the first quadrant inside the circle $x^2+y^2=8$ and outside the parabola $y^2=2 x$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zGPNO",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "gRgEj",
      "text": "$\\pi-\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LHAh9",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "4NdKo",
      "text": "$\\pi-\\frac{2}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/w6cOjvZpHTfjgYU43ogBZBYj1y3HwYhXP88O0qezktg.original.fullsize.png\"><br />Required area $=\\operatorname{Ar}($ circle from 0 to 2$)-$ $\\operatorname{ar}($ para from 0 to 2$)$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =\\int_0^2 \\sqrt{8-x^2} d x-\\int_0^2 \\sqrt{2 x} d x \\\\ & =\\left[\\frac{x}{2} \\sqrt{8-x^2}+\\frac{8}{2} \\sin ^{-1} \\frac{x}{2 \\sqrt{2}}\\right]_0^2-\\sqrt{2}\\left[\\frac{x \\sqrt{x}}{3 / 2}\\right]_0^2 \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{2} \\sqrt{8-4}+\\frac{8}{2} \\sin ^{-1} \\frac{2}{2 \\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2 \\sqrt{2}}{3}(2 \\sqrt{2}-0) \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 2+4 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{8}{3}=\\pi-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
